 "notes": [
  "Step 1 parts are unchanged: 4 jumper wires, because the speaker's own leads supply its two connections.",
  "The schematic labels the series resistor on pin 9 as 10K, but the parts list and circuit text say 100 ohm, so r2 is 100 ohm.",
  "Circuit: pin 9 goes through the 100 ohm resistor to one speaker terminal, and the other speaker terminal goes to GND. 5V goes to the photoresistor. The photoresistor's other leg joins A0 and the 4.7K resistor, and the 4.7K resistor goes to GND.",
  "Breadboard hole positions are read from the image and use the catalogue naming. Bank 't' is rows a-e and bank 'b' is rows f-j. The photoresistor sits at column 21 across the centre gap and the 100 ohm resistor sits at column 9 across the gap. The 4.7K resistor spans columns 21 to 24 in the lower half. The exact columns are approximate.",
  "The speaker has no marked polarity (symmetric 1=2). Its red lead goes to the breadboard (port 2) and its black lead goes to the Arduino GND pin beside AREF (GND.1). The other GND wire goes to GND.2 on the power header.",
  "Each physical connection has both a joined and an electrical edge."
